<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolt · War</p><h1 class="enc-title">War of the Golden Stool</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1900">1900</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The War of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/golden-stool">Golden Stool</a> was an <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ashanti-empire">Ashanti</a> uprising against British rule in 1900, also known as the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/yaa-asantewaa">Yaa Asantewaa</a> War. It was provoked when the British governor demanded to sit on the Golden Stool, the sacred symbol of Ashanti nationhood. Led by Yaa Asantewaa, it was the last major armed resistance to British rule in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/west-africa">West Africa</a>; after its suppression the Ashanti Empire was formally annexed as a British <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/crown-colony">Crown Colony</a> on 1 January 1902, though the Golden Stool itself was never captured.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/war-of-the-golden-stool.jpg" alt="War of the Golden Stool" width="302" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown author · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Typical_fight_in_the_forest,_Anglo-Ashanti_War_of_1900_(Battles_of_the_nineteenth_century,_1901).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
